1
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,620
Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:38,124
Yu-Gi-Oh!

3
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:03,797
I hope you're sitting down, Serenity,

4
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,237
because your big brother
had some pretty big news.

5
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,957
You made it to the Battle City Finals.

6
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,477
Wait, how'd you guess, sis?

7
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,795
Did Tristan tell you?

8
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:14,757
No, you're a great duelist, and I
knew all along you'd be a finalist.

9
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,140
I'm so proud of you.

10
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,500
Thanks, Serenity.

11
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,357
I couldn't have done it
without your support.

12
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:21,517
If it weren't for you and
my buddies cheering me on,

13
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,497
there's no way I would have
won these six locator cards.

14
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:28,168
I just wish you could have seen
old Joey in action, Serenity.

15
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:29,540
Well, guess what?

16
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,840
Uh, what, sis?

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,260
Maybe I still can.

18
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,287
It's not too late, you know.

19
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,212
What about the bandages?

20
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,734
I thought your eyes were still healing.

21
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:43,457
Well, the doctor said I could
take the bandages off tonight.

22
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:45,246
That means I can get my wish.

23
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:49,820
The next sight I see will be my big
bro dueling in the Battle City Finals.

24
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,190
That's great.

25
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,057
So it sounds like you can come home.

26
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:55,677
I'll send someone over to
pick you up right away.

27
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,957
I gotta prep for the finals, and
there's no way you're traveling alone.

28
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,460
I can't wait to see you.

29
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,050
Hooray!

30
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:05,530
Joey!

31
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,720
Joey, easy with the technology, you spaz.

32
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:12,657
Sorry, but Serenity takes
her bandages off tonight.

33
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:15,600
Wow, that's so awesome, Joey. Yeah.

34
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:18,220
And she's coming to the finals with us.

35
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,800
What wonderful news.

36
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,997
I just need someone to go pick her up.

37
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,120
Someone I can really depend on.

38
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:27,812
But where am I going to find
someone on such short notice?

39
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:34,140
I'll go and get her, you dimwit.

40
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,240
You, no way.

41
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:38,047
Don't worry, she'll be
in safe hands with me.

42
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,940
Hey, come back. Tristan.

43
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,000
Oh, well, Tristan is like family.

44
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:46,637
Kind of like that annoying
cousin who's always bugging you.

45
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,550
Oh, no, look.

46
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,160
It's Bakura, and he's hurt!

47
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,670
Bakura!

48
00:02:53,753 --> 00:02:54,583
What happened?

49
00:02:54,666 --> 00:02:56,697
I just found him lying on the ground.

50
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:58,192
He doesn't look so good.

51
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,576
I tried to take care of his injuries.

52
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:01,800
You know him?

53
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,017
He hasn't said a word since I found him.

54
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,957
We're buddies, but who do you
think could have done this?

55
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:07,870
Joey.

56
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,160
Bakura! What happened?

57
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,020
It happened so quickly.

58
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:13,440
I can't remember.

59
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,820
I'm lucky I found you all.

60
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:17,377
He needs to go to a hospital.

61
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:18,290
quickly.

62
00:03:18,373 --> 00:03:19,203
You're right.

63
00:03:19,286 --> 00:03:20,957
Sounds like Bakura's the lucky one.

64
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:23,099
I'll take him to see a doctor right

65
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,330
now.

66
00:03:24,413 --> 00:03:27,217
Joey, give me a hand.
Can do. There you go.

67
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,418
He'll be all right.

68
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,464
I'll call if there's some news.

69
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:33,970
All right.

70
00:03:34,053 --> 00:03:34,883
Best of luck.

71
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:35,796
See you later, Mr.

72
00:03:35,879 --> 00:03:36,709
Moto.

73
00:03:36,792 --> 00:03:37,622
Get that up, Bakura.

74
00:03:37,705 --> 00:03:39,177
My friends are in a great
deal of danger, Kaiba.

75
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,097
I hope you've led me to the right place.

76
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,010
Relax, Yugi.

77
00:03:42,093 --> 00:03:42,923
Your friends are here.

78
00:03:43,006 --> 00:03:43,836
Really?

79
00:03:43,919 --> 00:03:45,280
How can you be certain? Look,

80
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:48,177
KaibaCorp's satellite
tracking system traced Joey

81
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:51,017
Wheeler's dual disk to
these exact coordinates.

82
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,420
And it's foolproof.

83
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:58,232
Why Yugi cares about that
third-rate duelist is beyond me.

84
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,442
Soon he'll have bigger problems.

85
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,740
Hey, thanks a lot.

86
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,500
Uh, fella.

87
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:10,537
What he means to say is we
haven't introduced ourselves.

88
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:11,450
I'm Namu.

89
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:12,363
And you are?

90
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:15,300
The name's Joey. I'm Taya.

91
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,980
Thanks for all your help. Of course.

92
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,554
I just did what anyone would have done.

93
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,680
Is that a duel disc on your arm?

94
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,866
Yes, but I'm afraid I'm
not much of a duelist.

95
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,917
You're not challenging me
to a duel, are you, Joey?

96
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,176
I don't have to duel, because I
already qualified for the finals, Namu.

97
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,800
Wow, impressive.

98
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,260
You must be good.

99
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,657
Maybe you could give me some tips one day.

100
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:41,820
Well, I'll see if I can fit you in.

101
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:45,177
Hmm, I feel as though I've met you before.

102
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:46,848
Yeah, I know what you mean.

103
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:49,180
Smell you later, Namu.

104
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,615
Nice meeting you two.

105
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,157
Seems like a nice enough guy.

106
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,070
Totally.

107
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:59,760
Those fools have no idea who I really am
or the danger that's in store for them.

108
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:01,760
Listen, my rare hunters.

109
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,335
Everything is going according to plan.

110
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:07,457
So obey my orders and
don't fail me this time.

111
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:11,677
You must bring me the two remaining
Egyptian god cards and the

112
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:16,280
Millennium Puzzle and make sure that
little Yugi stays out of my way.

113
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:17,690
Permanently.

114
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:23,460
In order for me to obtain the
ultimate power of the Pharaoh,

115
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:26,249
everything must occur
exactly as I planned.

116
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,417
How shall we proceed, Master Maric?

117
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:33,440
Your task is to win me the two remaining
Egyptian god cards. Yes, Master.

118
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:37,092
Obtaining Obelisk the Tormentor
from Kaiba will be simple.

119
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:41,597
And winning Slifer the Sky Dragon from
Yugi will be equally as effortless.

120
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,856
We will not fail you, Master Merrick.

121
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:48,219
Don't underestimate the power of
these Egyptian god cards, you fools.

122
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,997
Defeating them will be difficult.

123
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:54,720
That's why I've devised an alternate
plan to ensure that I get what I want.

124
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:58,040
While you keep Kaiba and
little Yugi occupied,

125
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:01,458
I'll turn my attention to
those they care most about.

126
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,097
With their friends and
loved ones in danger,

127
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:06,740
I'll be sure to get exactly what I want,

128
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:10,216
and soon I'll be the most
powerful being in the world!

129
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,040
Hey, wait up!

130
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:14,580
Joey! Taya! What's up?

131
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,717
I don't mean to be an inconvenience,

132
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,397
but can you give me a few
dueling tips right now?

133
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,833
Sure, I can hit you with a few pointers.

134
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,857
Thanks, I'd like to win at
least one duel in Battle City.

135
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:26,777
You've come to the right place, Namu.

136
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:30,213
I got so many dueling secrets,
it'll make your head spin.

137
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,040
Joey! Taya!

138
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,700
They're not here. Kaibo was wrong.

139
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,500
Just stick with me, Namu.

140
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,597
You'll be a dueling expert in no time.

141
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,510
Wait!

142
00:06:43,593 --> 00:06:44,820
Joey, look behind you!

143
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,160
Take this! You got him!

144
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:48,280
Piece of cake!

145
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,880
Let go of her, you creep!

146
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,960
Look, what do you want?

147
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:55,080
You're real tough.

148
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,717
Why don't you pick on me?

149
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,680
Joey, behind you! You fool!

150
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,897
Are you all right? Joey!

151
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,260
I've been better.

152
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,099
Expecting someone?

153
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:08,480
I'll take that.

154
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,060
Get off of my stuff!

155
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:14,760
You heard her. Lay off! Hello,
Taya. Are you there? Hello?

156
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,240
Yogi, help!

157
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,740
Taya, where are you? No!

158
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,309
You're gonna pay for that.

159
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,820
Looks like your friend won't
find you now. Are you there?

160
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,860
Taya! Taya!

161
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:29,160
Oh, no.

162
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:35,480
Well, it appears that I've hit upon
your sensitive spot, haven't I now?

163
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:40,626
Perhaps I will use your friends to get
what I want from you, namely your puzzle.

164
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:44,280
And the Egyptian God card
that you won. Besides,

165
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,877
I'm always looking for new
servants to do my bidding,

166
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,960
and your friends will make
the perfect mine slaves.

167
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:52,450
Oh no.

168
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,702
I knew this was going to happen.

169
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:57,077
Merrick found my friends before I could.

170
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,840
But where did he take them?

171
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,390
Listen!

172
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:04,500
It seems we're too late, Kaiba.

173
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,800
The rare hunters have
already gotten to my friends.

174
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,480
Hey, Yugi, relax.

175
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:14,864
It's obvious they're really after
you and your Egyptian god card.

176
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,529
Not your pathetic friends.

177
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,447
They're of no use to anyone.

178
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:22,040
Besides, my satellite
will track them down.

179
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:25,137
Wheeler's dual disk sends
out a constant signal,

180
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,777
so finding your friends
will be a simple task.

181
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:31,820
And then, you're going
to duel against me, Yugi.

182
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:34,580
And your Egyptian God card will be mine.

183
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,140
So get ready to lose.

184
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:40,737
Kaiba, you and I will duel soon enough,
but not until my friends are safe.

185
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:41,880
Is that clear?

186
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:45,920
Seto, come in!

187
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,197
What is it, Mokuba?

188
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,317
We have a problem.

189
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:52,357
Joey Wheeler's duel disk isn't transmitting
a signal to the satellite system.

190
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,077
I think something's blocking it.

191
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:56,537
I'll go back to headquarters
and make sure the team

192
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:59,157
starts working on the
tracking problem right away.

193
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,070
Do it.

194
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,150
All right.

195
00:09:01,233 --> 00:09:02,497
We'll find those guys, Seto.

196
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:03,410
I promise.

197
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,420
When you do, let me know.

198
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,800
There's been a minor setback.

199
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,553
Either my satellite system has a glitch,

200
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:14,562
or these rare hunters are
smarter than I thought.

201
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,560
There he is.

202
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,640
Hey, who are you?

203
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,629
You're not going anywhere.

204
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:27,480
What's the rush?

205
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,340
You're ours now.

206
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,380
Leave me alone.

207
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,117
You're one of those rare
hunters, aren't you?

208
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,980
Perhaps I am, and today you're my prey.

209
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:44,437
I hear it's your last
day with us, Serenity.

210
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:47,755
The doctor said you can take
your bandages off tonight.

211
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,200
Yes, I can't wait.

212
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,117
I already know the first
thing I'm gonna see.

213
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,540
Yeah? And what's that?

214
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:56,060
Well, my brother Doolin.

215
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:59,257
He just told me he made it
to the Battle City Finals.

216
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,200
That's great.

217
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,977
Your brother must really
mean a lot to you.

218
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,977
He's lucky to have a sister like you.

219
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,640
I think I'm the lucky one.

220
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,134
I've got the best brother in the world.

221
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,480
There they are.

222
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:22,386
Yes, and it's time to lure them
to the chosen dueling location.

223
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,480
I'll be back.

224
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:37,900
Rare Hunter, what have
you done with my friends?

225
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,140
That's for us to know.

226
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:43,400
And Seto Kaiba, look who
else is coming with us.

227
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,440
Let him go!

228
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,090
Big brother!

229
00:10:51,173 --> 00:10:52,360
Help me, Seto!

230
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:54,160
Help me, please! Mokuba!

231
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,700
Seto, get me down!

232
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,800
Please help me, Seto! Mokuba!

233
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:06,320
Rare hunters, let my brother go now!

234
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:11,020
He's fine for now, but his
future's up in the air!

235
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:13,577
Help me, Seto!

236
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:14,900
They'll pay for this!

237
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:19,300
If you so much as touch one
hair on my brother's head,

238
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,717
I promise I'll hunt you all
down and crush every one

239
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:26,035
of you with the weight of
the entire Kaiba Corporation.

240
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,677
Your empty Cards will get you nowhere.

241
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:33,320
But there is one way to
save your brother. Tell me.

242
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,369
Meet us at the top of
that building, Kaiba.

243
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:42,240
That is, if you ever expect
to see your brother again.

244
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,160
The choice is yours.

245
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,150
Mokuba!

246
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:53,517
And Kaiba's not the only one
whose presence is required.

247
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:58,600
If you expect to be reunited with your
friends, you'll join us as well, Yugi.

248
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,610
Listen to me.

249
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,200
I'm warning you.

250
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:03,320
Leave them alone.

251
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,640
I'll see you both shortly.

252
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,972
Remember, gentlemen, meet us on the roof.

253
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,946
Looks like we have no choice.

254
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:14,870
That's right.

255
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:17,000
Our enemies are one and the same.

256
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,620
But make no mistake,
I'm in this for Mokuba.

257
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:26,039
When it comes to rescuing your
friends, you're on your own now, Yugi.

258
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,160
Fine, Kaiba.

259
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,380
I see you two decided to show up.

260
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:38,837
A very wise choice.

261
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:41,840
Yes, now tell us, what
is the meaning of this?

262
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,760
We've kept up our end of the deal,

263
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:48,017
so why don't you honor yours
and release the prisoners?

264
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,982
I'm afraid it isn't that simple.

265
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,097
You two will have to duel us first.

266
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:54,827
If you win, you'll see
your loved ones again.

267
00:12:56,760 --> 00:13:00,020
Before the fun begins, allow
us to introduce ourselves.

268
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:02,100
I am Loomis.

269
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,120
I am Umbra.

270
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:10,597
You defeated us once before, but I assure
you, you won't be so lucky in this duel.

271
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:13,457
And if we do win, you'll
release our friends and family?

272
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:16,260
Perhaps, but there's no way you'll win.

273
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:19,089
Now let me explain the
rules of this match.

274
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:23,520
It will be a double
duel, us against you two.

275
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:26,640
Each duelist will receive
4,000 life points.

276
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:30,517
You must defeat both of the other
team's duelists in order to win.

277
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:34,117
And as for the losers, they'll
pay a very hefty price.

278
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,040
A trip to the Shadow Realm.

279
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:41,580
You'll be delivered to the Dark
World in the most ingenious of ways.

280
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,377
Notice where you're standing.

281
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:45,937
On a thin surface above a 50-story light

282
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:48,517
shaft that runs all the
way to the ground floor.

283
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,500
But if you fall, you'll
never reach the bottom.

284
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:57,280
That's because the very surface on which
we stand is a divider between our world

285
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,837
and the dreaded Shadow Realm.

286
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,757
Each duelist's life
points will be displayed

287
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:06,557
in the magic shadow box
on the floor beside you.

288
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,581
When your life points reach zero,

289
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:10,597
the surface below you will be destroyed,

290
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:14,500
opening up a vortex that leads
directly to the Shadow Realm.

291
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,440
And according to Battle City rules,

292
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:26,500
your rules, when we win we take
your Egyptian god cards. Ready?

293
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,997
Looks like I've left you speechless.

294
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,057
I was just waiting for you to finish.

295
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:38,260
Do I have your guarantee
that my brother's all right?

296
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,586
Yes, but I wouldn't count
on seeing him again.

297
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:45,355
Once you're in the Shadow
Realm, there are no visitors.

298
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:51,440
It looks as if you've just made your
second mistake today, Rare Hunter.

299
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:56,060
The first was kidnapping my brother,
and the second was challenging me.

300
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,967
We'll see about that, Kaiba.

301
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:03,557
and i will rescue my
friends very touching but

302
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:06,817
we duel for our master
maric and losing is not an

303
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:09,797
option our decks were
specially assembled to take

304
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:12,557
down your egyptian god
cards and that's just what

305
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:15,757
we'll do and once we
deliver them to master maric

306
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:18,797
he'll possess all three
egyptian god cards in

307
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:21,217
the meantime you'll be
spending all of eternity

308
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:24,660
in the shadow realm so if
you're ready let's duel

309
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,900
Are you ready to duel?

310
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,340
I trust you know the rules.

311
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:35,580
Yes, this duel is two against two.

312
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,917
Each player takes a separate turn,

313
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:42,457
but players on the same team must work
together to defeat the opposing team.

314
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:43,700
And I'll begin.

315
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:45,333
Very well, Rare Hunter.

316
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:49,220
I'll place two cards face
down and end my turn.

317
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:51,540
Make your move if you dare.

318
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:55,260
It'll only bring you closer
to the Shadow Realm. Roll!

319
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:00,460
I'll summon Beta, the Magnet
Warrior, in defense mode.

320
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:05,436
My monster will protect my life points
from your attacks, rare hunters.

321
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:10,888
No one can attack until each
duelist has drawn at least once.

322
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:14,020
Hopefully by then, I can
pick up on their strategy.

323
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,190
Observe.

324
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:19,460
I summon Shining Abyss in defense mode.

325
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:24,645
Now it's time to show
you how we duel together.

326
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:26,460
A team strategy.

327
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:27,938
That's right, Yugi.

328
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,748
Activate Mask of Brutality.

329
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,900
Thank you, Loomis.

330
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:35,785
Your mask will be a
perfect fit for my monster.

331
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,420
Not only that, Oprah,

332
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:50,177
but it will boost your monster's
attack power by a thousand points.

333
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:51,090
What?

334
00:16:51,173 --> 00:16:55,177
These rare hunters already have a monster
on the field with 2,600 attack points.

335
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:56,090
That's right,

336
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:59,277
and it will stay that way as
long as we each give up 1,000

337
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:02,889
life points for every turn we
plan to use Mask of Brutality.

338
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:05,460
But now we won't have to.

339
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,540
Observe, as I activate a
magic card called Masked Doll.

340
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:19,320
My Masked Doll will absorb any and all
negative effects caused by my magic card.

341
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:21,640
Nice work.

342
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:25,717
Now our life points will remain
untouched by our mask of brutality.

343
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:27,565
You fools are no match for us.

344
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,420
Yes, that's right.

345
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:33,280
And our tag team strategy
will destroy you. I doubt it.

346
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,357
We can play off the
strengths of each other's

347
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:37,877
cards and work as a
team as well as you can,

348
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,790
rare hunters.

349
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,280
No thanks.

350
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:44,699
Teamwork is for boy scouts
in nursery schools, Yugi.

351
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:45,850
You're wrong.

352
00:17:45,933 --> 00:17:47,566
Let's get one thing straight.

353
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:50,857
I can win this duel and save
my brother without your help.

354
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:52,617
I'm the world's greatest duelist,

355
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:55,637
and when I win the Battle City
Tournament, I'll prove it.

356
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,640
And now, stand back.

357
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:01,720
I'll place two cards face down.

358
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:05,097
And then...

359
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:08,040
I'll summon Force Raider the Man Beast.

360
00:18:13,180 --> 00:18:16,000
And I place my monster in attack mode.

361
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:19,540
What's he doing?

362
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,197
His monster's weaker than theirs!

363
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:24,257
And if we don't have a team
strategy, we'll never win!

364
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:25,170
Excellent.

365
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:28,280
I've got an extremely
powerful monster ready to go.

366
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:33,240
Next turn, I'll sacrifice my Virus Raider
and summon it to the field. Teamwork.

367
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:35,857
Well, we've each taken one turn.

368
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,764
Now it's time to see whose
strategy is superior.

369
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:41,537
I think you'll find the
answer to that is obvious.

370
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:42,450
I agree.

371
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:46,897
Due to our team's strategy, we have
the most powerful monster on the field.

372
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:49,897
Might I remind you our decks
were specifically created

373
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:53,260
to work together to defeat
your Egyptian god cards.

374
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:55,780
This duel has just begun, Rare Hunters.

375
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,920
We have to win.

376
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,197
The safety of my friends depends on it.

377
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:02,137
But unless Kaiba agrees to work
together as a team, we're doomed.

378
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:04,600
If he keeps up this selfish attitude,

379
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:07,817
we'll lose this duel and be
transported to the Shadow Realm.

380
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:10,757
And Merrick will have all
three Egyptian god cards.

381
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:14,337
Plus, who knows what will happen to
the gang under Merrick's control?

382
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:16,714
We've got to defeat these rare hunters,

383
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:20,080
the fate of my friends, and
the world depends on it.

384
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,019
You're the only one who's competing
